{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the opening for its head shall be in its midst.</b> It seems to me that what they expounded — 'let a matter of voice come and atone for the matter of voice' — is further inclusive of all who speak falsehoods and deal falsely in their speech, and have burning lips and an evil heart; for therefore the robe (מעיל) is called by that name, because it comes to atone for dealing falsely (מעיל). Therefore He commanded concerning the robe: ״והיה פי ראשו בתוכו״ — 'and the opening for its head shall be in its midst.'" "<b>And there is</b> in this an allusion and admonition to a person, that it is fitting for him that his speech be equal to what is within him — that his inward part be as his outward part — and that his lip be as the opening for his head, woven all around, to hold back words. But he does not do so; rather, the deed of a weaver folds his words double, like this weave that folds the threads of its weaving, and likewise the כפי תחרא as the כפי השריון, whose rings are doubled. Therefore the robe comes to atone for this sin, for it is far from the HaShem, blessed be He, and 'a speaker of falsehoods shall not be established before His eyes.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:14.701659323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}